From 2d858a3152a2e1fed0f5742233574da1763974f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Murka-Moncz Zsigmond <sanyikapenz@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:32:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Use hassh64 for the name table hash

Replace the byte-at-a-time FNV-1a in hash_string() with hassh64 (MIT,
single header, vendored as src/util/hassh.h with its license notice),
truncated to the existing 32-bit Name::hash. The signature, the table
layout and every caller stay the same.

hassh64 reads 8 bytes at a time, so its cost barely grows with the key
length, while FNV-1a has a multiply in the dependency chain per byte.
Measured on the identifier tokens of the preprocessed sqlite3.c
amalgamation (207,025 tokens, mean length 5.7), gcc -O2, one core:

  length   tokens   FNV-1a    hassh64
  1-4      102,865  4.1 ns    5.0 ns
  5-8       71,863  4.8 ns    2.4 ns
  9-16      20,448  6.4 ns    2.9 ns
  17-44     11,849  9.4 ns    2.5 ns
  all      207,025  6.2 ns    5.9 ns

Hashing is a small part of compile time, so whole compiles do not move
beyond noise (best of 15, taskset -c 3): sqlite3.c with xcc -c 571.7 ms
vs 569.5 ms, xcc's own 38 sources 278.7 ms vs 278.5 ms. The generated
assembly for sqlite3.c is identical apart from local label numbering.

When built by gcc/clang for x86-64 without -maes the header selects its
AES-NI path at run time; xcc and wcc themselves (self-hosting) get the
portable C path. The header adds about 19 KB of text to each gcc-built
executable and about 57 KB to each self-hosted one.

make test, test-gen2, test-ssa, test-wcc and test-wcc-gen2 pass.
---
 src/util/table.c | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/util/table.c b/src/util/table.c
index 5b0014a..9b36ea7 100644
--- a/src/util/table.c
+++ b/src/util/table.c
@@ -4,15 +4,13 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>  // malloc
 #include <string.h>
 
+#include "hassh.h"
+
 // Hash
 
 static uint32_t hash_string(const char *key, int length) {
-  const unsigned char *u = (const unsigned char*)key;
-  // FNV1a
-  uint32_t hash = 2166136261u;
-  for (int i = 0; i < length; ++i)
-    hash = (hash ^ u[i]) * 16777619u;
-  return hash;
+  // hassh64, truncated to the table's 32-bit hash.
+  return (uint32_t)hassh64(key, length, 0);
 }
 
 // Name
-- 
